# Festie backend environment example — copy to .env and fill in real values.
# Only secrets/config that are not safe to commit live here. Never commit a real .env.

# ── Apple Push Notification service (APNs) — iOS direct push ────────────────
# expo-notifications getDevicePushTokenAsync() returns a RAW APNs device token
# on iOS, which firebase-admin (FCM) cannot send. These enable a direct APNs/2
# sender for iOS device tokens. All optional: if APNS_KEY_PATH / APNS_KEY_ID are
# unset, APNs is disabled and iOS tokens are SKIPPED (never deleted).
#
# APNS_KEY_PATH   Absolute path to the APNs Auth Key .p8 file (downloaded once
#                 from the Apple Developer portal → Keys). Path only — the key
#                 file itself must NOT be committed.
# APNS_KEY_ID     The 10-char Key ID shown next to the key in the Apple portal.
# APNS_TEAM_ID    Apple Developer Team ID (defaults to J63QL8R63J).
# APNS_BUNDLE_ID  iOS app bundle id / APNs topic (defaults to us.festie.app).
# APNS_PRODUCTION true = api.push.apple.com (App Store / TestFlight builds),
#                 false = api.sandbox.push.apple.com (local Xcode dev builds).
#                 Defaults to true. TestFlight uses the PRODUCTION gateway.
#APNS_KEY_PATH=/etc/festie/apns/AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8
#APNS_KEY_ID=XXXXXXXXXX
#APNS_TEAM_ID=J63QL8R63J
#APNS_BUNDLE_ID=us.festie.app
#APNS_PRODUCTION=true
